# Lekcja s22_extras / Ext05WebFluxOverview — WebFlux (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
# 1. Uruchom Ext05Application (▶ obok main). W logu: „Netty started on port 8080” (nie Tomcat!).
# 2. Kliknij ▶ obok zapytania.

@host = http://localhost:8080

### 1. Flux → tablica JSON — oczekiwane: 200 OK, 4 produkty
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/products

### 2. Mono → obiekt JSON — oczekiwane: 200 OK, {"sku":"SPO-001","name":"Kawa ziarnista 1kg","price":64.99,"stock":120}
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/products/SPO-001

### 3. Puste Mono → 404 — oczekiwane: 404 Not Found, JSON z "status":404 i "requestId"
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/products/XXX-999

### 4. Styl funkcyjny (RouterFunction) — oczekiwane: 200 OK, text/plain „Cześć z WebFlux!”
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/hello

### 5. PUŁAPKA: block() na wątku Netty — oczekiwane: 500 Internal Server Error; w logu aplikacji
#    IllegalStateException: block()/blockFirst()/blockLast() are blocking, which is not supported in thread reactor-http-nio-N
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/products/ELE-001/blocking-stock

### 6. Blokujący kod przeniesiony na boundedElastic — oczekiwane: 200 OK, {"sku":"ELE-001","price":4399.99,"thread":"boundedElastic-1"}
GET {{host}}/api/reactive/products/ELE-001/wholesale-price
